# "Return one or two target creatures and/or enchantments you own": ownership, not control (the rulings: "can target any creatures and/or enchantments you own, including ones controlled
# by other players"). On turn 2 Bot2's kicked Thieving Skydiver (X = 1) takes Bot1's Ornithopter (mana value 0). On turn 3 Bot1 can target the Ornithopter - it owns it - but not
# Bot2's own Skydiver or Ornithopter (the refusals), and returns it to its hand; Bot2 keeps the Skydiver and its own Ornithopter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Get Out
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Thieving Skydiver
Ornithopter
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Thieving Skydiver.Cast(Kicked: 1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Get Out.Cast
Bot1.Modes(2)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Thieving Skydiver)
! Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Hand = Ornithopter; Island; Island; Island; Island; Island
Bot1.Graveyard = Get Out; Black Lotus
Bot2.Battlefield = Island; Mox Sapphire; Mox Jet; Thieving Skydiver; Ornithopter
